   "versionNonce": 52259875,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1735689600000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "- Each act reads left to right: what is tried, the control that decides, and the result. Red results are refusals (or the legacy leak); the chips under each panel name the walls it exercises.\n- Different acts stop the request at different walls: the gateway (W1), the MCP server (W2), the data plane (W3) and the guardrail (W0). Act 2 proves keys are off, and Act 5 shows how\n  the evidence joins up.\n- Act 7 runs as real people: a different answer per persona, the agent's front door, the bill and a live token budget. A persona that has not signed in once shows design, a predicted\n  result and not a run.",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "- Each act reads left to right: what is tried, the control that decides, and the result. Red results are refusals (or the legacy leak); the chips under each panel name the walls it exercises.\n- Different acts stop the request at different walls: the gateway (W1), the MCP server (W2), the data plane (W3) and the guardrail (W0). Act 2 proves keys are off, and Act 5 shows how\n  the evidence joins up.\n- Act 7 runs as real people: a different answer per persona, the agent's front door, the bill and a live token budget. A persona that has not signed in once shows design, a predicted\n  result and not a run.",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
